1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,016
You wake up in your own room, in the
middle of the night,

2
00:00:04,036 --> 00:00:08,219
because something close to your bed has
made a sound.

3
00:00:08,239 --> 00:00:11,856
You open your eyes and you see only black.

4
00:00:11,876 --> 00:00:14,469
You lie still and you listen.

5
00:00:14,489 --> 00:00:19,080
Then your eyes begin to work in the dark,
and you understand

6
00:00:19,100 --> 00:00:22,912
that the black above you is not the
ceiling.

7
00:00:22,932 --> 00:00:26,800
It is two empty holes, in a face with no
eyes,

8
00:00:26,820 --> 00:00:30,631
leaning over you, close enough to touch.

9
00:00:30,651 --> 00:00:36,631
Something dark is running out of those
holes and down the side of its face.

10
00:00:36,651 --> 00:00:41,113
This is the story of the thing people call
Eyeless Jack.

11
00:00:41,133 --> 00:00:42,896
Let us go back to the beginning.

12
00:00:43,496 --> 00:00:47,651
My name is Mitch, and until a few years
ago I did

13
00:00:47,671 --> 00:00:51,679
not believe in anything I could not touch.

14
00:00:51,699 --> 00:00:53,947
I lost my house that spring.

15
00:00:53,967 --> 00:00:59,802
The bank took it, the way banks do, slowly
and then all at once.

16
00:00:59,822 --> 00:01:04,542
My older brother Edwin called me the same
week and told

17
00:01:04,562 --> 00:01:09,302
me to stop being proud and come and live
with him.

18
00:01:09,322 --> 00:01:13,343
We had not seen each other properly in ten
years,

19
00:01:13,363 --> 00:01:17,174
so part of me was actually glad about it.

20
00:01:17,194 --> 00:01:23,749
His house was one of those cheap places at
the end of a long street, with a

21
00:01:23,769 --> 00:01:30,599
wooden porch, a bare back yard, and pine
woods standing behind the fence.

22
00:01:30,619 --> 00:01:32,739
It took me a week to unpack.

23
00:01:32,759 --> 00:01:38,960
Boxes in the hall, boxes on the landing,
boxes down the side of the bed.

24
00:01:38,980 --> 00:01:42,943
"Take the back room. It is quiet, and the
window gets the morning."

25
00:01:42,963 --> 00:01:44,870
The back room was quiet.

26
00:01:44,890 --> 00:01:47,673
That is the part I think about now.

27
00:01:47,693 --> 00:01:49,944
I slept well that first week.

28
00:01:49,964 --> 00:01:55,662
I remember thinking that this was the
first time in a year that I had felt safe.

29
00:01:56,262 --> 00:02:00,372
About a week in, I woke up at one in the
morning.

30
00:02:00,392 --> 00:02:04,621
There was a sound coming from outside,
under the window.

31
00:02:04,641 --> 00:02:07,983
A slow, careful rustling, the way
something

32
00:02:08,003 --> 00:02:11,561
moves when it does not want to be heard.

33
00:02:11,581 --> 00:02:15,398
I lay there and listened to it for a long
time.

34
00:02:15,418 --> 00:02:19,189
I told myself it was a raccoon in the
bins.

35
00:02:19,209 --> 00:02:20,656
We had raccoons.

36
00:02:20,676 --> 00:02:24,033
Everybody on that street had raccoons.

37
00:02:24,053 --> 00:02:27,580
So I turned over and I went back to sleep.

38
00:02:27,600 --> 00:02:31,851
In the morning I told Edwin about it over
his coffee.

39
00:02:31,871 --> 00:02:36,524
"Raccoons. They get into everything out
here. I will put a brick on the bin lid."

40
00:02:36,544 --> 00:02:41,498
He put a brick on the bin lid, and we both
forgot about it.

41
00:02:41,518 --> 00:02:44,508
I want you to notice how easy that was.

42
00:02:44,528 --> 00:02:50,703
A noise outside, a simple answer, and a
man can sleep for one more night.

43
00:02:51,303 --> 00:02:53,735
The next night was different.

44
00:02:53,755 --> 00:02:55,697
I did not wake up slowly.

45
00:02:55,717 --> 00:03:00,258
I came awake all at once, the way you do
when a sound

46
00:03:00,278 --> 00:03:04,494
belongs inside your room and not outside
it.

47
00:03:04,514 --> 00:03:09,456
I was almost sure I had heard my window
being lifted open.

48
00:03:09,476 --> 00:03:13,248
And then a thump, soft and heavy, like a
person

49
00:03:13,268 --> 00:03:17,168
landing on the floor with their knees
bent.

50
00:03:17,188 --> 00:03:21,824
I sat straight up and I looked at every
corner of that room.

51
00:03:21,844 --> 00:03:23,398
The window was shut.

52
00:03:23,418 --> 00:03:25,897
The boxes were where I had left them.

53
00:03:25,917 --> 00:03:27,362
Nothing moved.

54
00:03:27,382 --> 00:03:30,836
I listened until my ears were ringing with
the

55
00:03:30,856 --> 00:03:34,533
effort, and the house gave me nothing
back.

56
00:03:34,553 --> 00:03:38,507
After a while I told myself I had been
dreaming,

57
00:03:38,527 --> 00:03:42,766
and I lay down again with my back to the
wall.

58
00:03:42,786 --> 00:03:43,846
I slept.

59
00:03:43,866 --> 00:03:49,084
That is the thing I cannot explain to
anybody who has not been through it.

60
00:03:49,104 --> 00:03:49,884
I slept.

61
00:03:50,484 --> 00:03:56,046
The next morning I walked into the
kitchen, and Edwin dropped his cup.

62
00:03:56,066 --> 00:04:00,992
It hit the floor and broke and he did not
even look at it.

63
00:04:01,012 --> 00:04:03,042
He was looking at my face.

64
00:04:03,062 --> 00:04:05,909
"Mitch. Do not touch it. Just stand
there."

65
00:04:05,929 --> 00:04:12,109
He took the little mirror off the shelf by
the door and held it up in front of me.

66
00:04:12,129 --> 00:04:14,844
There was a long cut down my left cheek.

67
00:04:14,864 --> 00:04:21,675
Clean, straight, and nothing like a
scratch from a nail or a corner of a box.

68
00:04:21,695 --> 00:04:23,252
I had not felt it.

69
00:04:23,272 --> 00:04:27,882
I had slept through the whole night and I
had not felt a thing.

70
00:04:27,902 --> 00:04:31,817
Edwin drove me to the hospital with both
hands

71
00:04:31,837 --> 00:04:35,003
tight on the wheel and the radio off.

72
00:04:35,603 --> 00:04:40,381
The doctor cleaned the cut and asked me
the questions they ask.

73
00:04:40,401 --> 00:04:43,744
"Do you drink before bed? Do you take
anything to sleep?

74
00:04:43,764 --> 00:04:47,437
Has anyone in your family ever walked in
their sleep?"

75
00:04:47,457 --> 00:04:51,885
I said no to all of it, and he wrote it
down anyway.

76
00:04:51,905 --> 00:04:55,697
"The most likely answer is that you did
this to yourself while

77
00:04:55,717 --> 00:04:59,345
you were asleep. It happens more than
people think."

78
00:04:59,365 --> 00:05:01,345
I was ready to believe him.

79
00:05:01,365 --> 00:05:03,197
I wanted to believe him.

80
00:05:03,217 --> 00:05:07,274
A sleepwalking man is a problem you can
fix.

81
00:05:07,294 --> 00:05:10,978
Then he stopped writing, and his face
changed,

82
00:05:10,998 --> 00:05:15,132
and he asked me to lie back and lift my
shirt.

83
00:05:15,152 --> 00:05:18,657
He did not say anything for a long moment.

84
00:05:18,677 --> 00:05:21,944
"Mitch. There is a surgical cut in your
side, and it

85
00:05:21,964 --> 00:05:25,429
has been closed again with stitches. Neat
ones."

86
00:05:25,449 --> 00:05:30,517
He turned the screen of the scanner round
so that I could see it myself.

87
00:05:30,537 --> 00:05:34,035
I am not a doctor and even I could see
that there

88
00:05:34,055 --> 00:05:37,715
was a space where something should have
been.

89
00:05:37,735 --> 00:05:40,715
"You have lost your left kidney. Some time
last

90
00:05:40,735 --> 00:05:43,655
night. I am sorry. We do not know how."

91
00:05:43,675 --> 00:05:47,005
I remember the sound of the clock on that
wall.

92
00:05:47,025 --> 00:05:50,518
I remember a trolley going past the door.

93
00:05:50,538 --> 00:05:56,719
I remember the word last night, sitting in
the middle of the room like a stone.

94
00:05:56,739 --> 00:06:01,372
Somebody had opened me up while I slept,
taken a piece of me

95
00:06:01,392 --> 00:06:06,398
out, closed me again, and gone back out
through the window.

96
00:06:06,418 --> 00:06:12,654
This story is my own retelling of the
creepypasta Eyeless

97
00:06:12,674 --> 00:06:17,722
Jack, first posted by a user called
Azelf5000.

98
00:06:18,322 --> 00:06:22,234
They kept me in for the day and sent me
home with

99
00:06:22,254 --> 00:06:26,616
painkillers and a sheet of paper about
infection.

100
00:06:26,636 --> 00:06:31,765
Edwin wanted me to sleep on the couch,
downstairs, near him.

101
00:06:31,785 --> 00:06:35,181
I said I would be fine in the back room.

102
00:06:35,201 --> 00:06:37,022
I was not being brave.

103
00:06:37,042 --> 00:06:38,998
I think I wanted to know.

104
00:06:39,018 --> 00:06:43,747
I lay in that bed with the lamp off and
the painkillers

105
00:06:43,767 --> 00:06:48,687
moving in my blood, and at some point I
fell asleep.

106
00:06:48,707 --> 00:06:53,274
Around midnight I opened my eyes, and it
was there.

107
00:06:53,294 --> 00:06:57,969
It was standing over my bed, bent forward
at the waist, close

108
00:06:57,989 --> 00:07:02,652
enough that I could feel the air move when
it breathed.

109
00:07:02,672 --> 00:07:05,197
A black hooded top, the hood up.

110
00:07:05,217 --> 00:07:11,950
A face the colour of old grey paint, with
no nose and no mouth at all.

111
00:07:11,970 --> 00:07:15,650
And where the eyes should have been there
were two black

112
00:07:15,670 --> 00:07:19,469
holes that went back further than a face
should go.

113
00:07:19,489 --> 00:07:24,264
Something dark was running slowly out of
both of them, down what

114
00:07:24,284 --> 00:07:29,060
would have been its cheeks, and dripping
on to my blanket.

115
00:07:29,080 --> 00:07:30,608
I did not scream.

116
00:07:30,628 --> 00:07:35,251
I want to be honest about that, because
people always ask.

117
00:07:35,271 --> 00:07:37,209
I did not make a sound.

118
00:07:37,229 --> 00:07:41,211
My hand went sideways, on its own, to the
little

119
00:07:41,231 --> 00:07:44,996
shelf by the bed where I kept my camera.

120
00:07:45,016 --> 00:07:48,100
I lifted it, and I took the picture.

121
00:07:48,120 --> 00:07:54,053
The flash filled that room for half a
second, and in that half a second

122
00:07:54,073 --> 00:07:59,952
I saw all of it at once, every fold of the
hood and every finger.

123
00:07:59,972 --> 00:08:03,649
Then the dark came back, and it came at
me.

124
00:08:03,669 --> 00:08:09,955
It was fast, and it was strong, and it
went for my chest with both hands.

125
00:08:09,975 --> 00:08:14,605
I got my foot up between us and I kicked
it in the face

126
00:08:14,625 --> 00:08:19,198
as hard as a man with stitches can kick
anything.

127
00:08:19,218 --> 00:08:25,172
It went backwards into the boxes and I was
out of that bed and through the door.

128
00:08:25,772 --> 00:08:28,732
I grabbed my wallet off the hall table.

129
00:08:28,752 --> 00:08:30,264
I do not know why.

130
00:08:30,284 --> 00:08:32,169
You do strange things.

131
00:08:32,189 --> 00:08:36,900
I went out of the front door in bare feet
and I ran down

132
00:08:36,920 --> 00:08:41,827
that long street with the porch lights
going past me.

133
00:08:41,847 --> 00:08:43,793
I did not shout for Edwin.

134
00:08:43,813 --> 00:08:45,668
I did not go back for him.

135
00:08:45,688 --> 00:08:48,514
I have had a long time to think about
that.

136
00:08:48,534 --> 00:08:52,135
At the end of the street I went over the
fence

137
00:08:52,155 --> 00:08:55,892
and into the pine woods behind the houses.

138
00:08:55,912 --> 00:08:58,558
There was no moon under those trees.

139
00:08:58,578 --> 00:09:03,981
There was no path either, and I was
running on roots and stones.

140
00:09:04,001 --> 00:09:07,966
I remember the cold, and my own breath,
and the

141
00:09:07,986 --> 00:09:12,147
stitches in my side pulling with every
step.

142
00:09:12,167 --> 00:09:18,681
I remember looking back once and seeing
nothing at all, which was somehow worse.

143
00:09:18,701 --> 00:09:22,585
Then my foot caught a rock and the ground
came up

144
00:09:22,605 --> 00:09:26,429
and hit me, and the woods went out like a
light.

145
00:09:27,029 --> 00:09:34,011
I woke up in a hospital bed with a drip in
my arm and daylight on the wall.

146
00:09:34,031 --> 00:09:35,734
It was the same doctor.

147
00:09:35,754 --> 00:09:39,785
He came in with my notes under his arm and
he sat

148
00:09:39,805 --> 00:09:44,038
down, which nobody does when the news is
good.

149
00:09:44,058 --> 00:09:47,284
"There is good news and bad news, Mitch."

150
00:09:47,304 --> 00:09:51,023
"The good news is that you were lucky.
Cuts, bruises, a mild

151
00:09:51,043 --> 00:09:55,088
concussion. Your parents are on their way
to collect you."

152
00:09:55,108 --> 00:09:59,784
I let out a breath I think I had been
holding since midnight.

153
00:09:59,804 --> 00:10:03,263
"The bad news is that your brother was
found in the house

154
00:10:03,283 --> 00:10:06,520
this morning. He was killed. I am very
sorry."

155
00:10:06,540 --> 00:10:07,928
"Killed by what?"

156
00:10:07,948 --> 00:10:12,137
He looked at the floor, and then he looked
at me, and he

157
00:10:12,157 --> 00:10:16,420
told me the truth, which was that nobody
could say.

158
00:10:16,440 --> 00:10:20,408
I had kicked it in the face and run out of
the house,

159
00:10:20,428 --> 00:10:24,169
and it had not followed me into those
woods.

160
00:10:24,189 --> 00:10:25,871
It had not needed to.

161
00:10:25,891 --> 00:10:28,568
There was already somebody in that house.

162
00:10:29,168 --> 00:10:34,197
Three days later my parents drove me back
to get my things.

163
00:10:34,217 --> 00:10:36,105
They waited in the car.

164
00:10:36,125 --> 00:10:39,689
My mother did not want to go in and my
father did

165
00:10:39,709 --> 00:10:43,284
not want to leave her out there on her
own.

166
00:10:43,304 --> 00:10:47,210
The porch light was still on in the middle
of the day.

167
00:10:47,230 --> 00:10:49,337
Edwin always forgot it.

168
00:10:49,357 --> 00:10:54,100
I went up the stairs to the back room and
I made myself calm,

169
00:10:54,120 --> 00:10:59,314
the way you do when you have practised
being calm in the car.

170
00:10:59,334 --> 00:11:04,038
My camera was still on the shelf where my
hand had left it.

171
00:11:04,058 --> 00:11:06,125
I put it in my pocket.

172
00:11:06,145 --> 00:11:10,437
And then I stopped, because I could see
along the hallway

173
00:11:10,457 --> 00:11:14,065
from there, and the hallway was not empty.

174
00:11:14,085 --> 00:11:20,336
I am not going to describe what the police
had already photographed in that house.

175
00:11:20,356 --> 00:11:25,852
My brother was at the far end of it, and
that is all I will say.

176
00:11:25,872 --> 00:11:28,962
There was something small lying on the
floor

177
00:11:28,982 --> 00:11:32,240
beside him, wrapped in a piece of cloth.

178
00:11:32,260 --> 00:11:35,725
I picked it up without thinking, the way
you pick

179
00:11:35,745 --> 00:11:39,304
up anything that does not belong on a
floor.

180
00:11:39,324 --> 00:11:43,861
I carried it out past my mother and my
father and I sat

181
00:11:43,881 --> 00:11:48,703
down in the back seat of their car with it
in my lap.

182
00:11:48,723 --> 00:11:52,687
We were two streets away before I opened
the cloth.

183
00:11:52,707 --> 00:11:58,247
It was the piece of me that had been taken
out of my side four nights before.

184
00:11:58,267 --> 00:11:59,839
Some of it was gone.

185
00:11:59,859 --> 00:12:04,635
There was a dark stain on the cloth around
it, the same colour

186
00:12:04,655 --> 00:12:09,727
as the stuff that had been running out of
those empty holes.

187
00:12:09,747 --> 00:12:17,103
I was sick in my mother's car, and then I
cried, and my father did not stop driving.

188
00:12:17,123 --> 00:12:19,793
The picture is still on that camera.

189
00:12:19,813 --> 00:12:24,276
I have never shown it to anybody who did
not ask twice.

190
00:12:24,296 --> 00:12:29,141
It is dark, and it is blurred, because my
hand was shaking.

191
00:12:29,161 --> 00:12:34,816
But the hood is there, and the face is
there, and the two holes are there.

192
00:12:34,836 --> 00:12:37,786
And there is one more thing in that
photograph

193
00:12:37,806 --> 00:12:40,604
that I have never been able to explain.

194
00:12:40,624 --> 00:12:42,881
The thing is not looking at me.

195
00:12:42,901 --> 00:12:47,707
It is looking past my shoulder, at the
door of my room, which

196
00:12:47,727 --> 00:12:52,825
I had left open, and which leads to the
rest of that house.

197
00:12:52,845 --> 00:12:54,605
Would you have taken the photograph?

